      "content": "The argument that \"doing nothing\" is cheaper is a dangerous fallacy because it ignores the catastrophic, irreversible costs of climate change that will eventually destroy our economy regardless of current regulations. We cannot afford to gamble our future on the idea that the planet will save itself, especially when the real cost of inaction is a global collapse that will wipe out all industries, including manufacturing. Instead of accepting these regulations as inevitable, we should demand a complete overhaul of the policy to ensure it actually protects the environment without strangling our local jobs.",
